// Analyzed file list for pulp_stream_xbar_order. Paths are relative to the
// PACKAGE ROOT: the elaboration recipe is sourced with the package root as cwd
// and `slang` is run from there too, so one spelling serves both.
//
// The round appends one `../submission/<worker>.sv` line per worker to the end
// of this file (v5/round.py), which resolves to <run_root>/submission from the
// same cwd. Do not add a trailing `-y`/library directive after the file list --
// an appended source line has to stay a source line.
//
// ONE analyzed file. The nine common-cells RTL files are NOT listed: `ft/tb.sv`
// pulls them in with `include at file scope, in dependency order and with
// `COMMON_CELLS_ASSERTS_OFF` already defined, exactly as the upstream task's
// `tcl/setup.tcl` does. Listing them as well would declare every module twice,
// and would also compile `cc_pkg.sv` outside the order the rest depends on.

// --- one Slang-only switch, and why it is here rather than in the source ----
// `ft/tb.sv` writes three variables from two processes:
//
//   past_valid   `initial past_valid = 1'b0;` (line 171) and the `always_ff`
//                (line 174). This is the ordinary formal idiom for a
//                past-valid flag and every FPV tool takes it.
//   s, d         the loop counters, declared once as `integer` and reused by
//                BOTH the `always_comb` that computes `target_ok` and the
//                `always_ff` that maintains the reference rings. Each block
//                assigns them before reading them, so neither can see the
//                other's value.
//
// Slang promotes `multiple-always-assigns` to an ERROR and will not elaborate
// the package without this line, which fails the `v6_dataset/elab_local.py`
// gate. Jasper takes all three.
//
// It lives here because this list is the only channel to Slang:
// `taskdefs.slang_args` copies every non-comment line into
// `lists/tc_elab.files.slang` and passes that with `-f`. Jasper's `analyze -f`
// does not understand `-W`, so `lists/tc_elab.tcl` reads this list itself and
// drops any line starting with `-` before calling `analyze`. That is one place
// deciding it, and it is documented at both ends.
//
// The alternative was editing `ft/tb.sv` to give the two blocks their own loop
// counters. It was rejected: the reference model IS the task's statement of
// what it is checking, and a package whose checker is not the upstream checker
// is a different experiment.
-Wno-multiple-always-assigns

// `+incdir+rtl` does double duty: it resolves the nine includes above AND the
// `common_cells/assertions.svh`, `common_cells/registers.svh` and
// `common_cells/deprecated/registers.svh` headers the RTL includes by that
// exact prefixed path.
+incdir+rtl

// --- the buffered 4x4 crossbar, the 16 reference rings, the target ----------
ft/tb.sv

// --- phase-1 candidate targets, bound into the formal top -------------------
// LAST, because a `bind` has to be analyzed after the module it binds into.
// `pulp_analyze_arguments` in lists/tc_elab.tcl drops the two comment lines
// above and passes this one through to `analyze` as a source, in this order.
sva/targets_pulp_stream_xbar_order.sv
